    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38893" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prō-pexus</span></b> , a, um,
			Part. [pecto], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>combed forward</i>, <i>combed down in
				front</i>, <i>hanging down</i> (<b>poet.</b>): crines, Att. ap. <i><span class="en">Serv.
				Verg. A. 12, 605</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">propexam in pectore barbam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 838</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">propexam ad pectora barbam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					1, 259</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">propexa mento Canities,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 97</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">propexis in pectora barbis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					13, 310</span></i>
			.</div>
